      "worked_solution": "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/assets/384610cdc149e8b4eaa6df1d3eea1715dda88543c57679553875d226814f6cf7.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(-1,4)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(1,2).$\n\nTherefore, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-4}{1-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{2} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
